Popular password management app 1Password today announced 1Password for Agents, a platform that gives AI agents safe access to user credentials for completing tasks.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Introducing 1Password for Agents" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/-1SE6cBbeZg" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
The platform lets AI agents access logins, passwords, and other data without seeing or storing the information. Agents can send a request to sign in to a website or account, and users can approve or deny the request. 1Password says the agent uses a unique digital key to verify its identity, and then the login information is filled directly into the sign-in form.<br/>
<br/>
Personal AI agents like Meta Muse, ChatGPT Dots, and Claude Duet often need access to accounts and sensitive user information, and 1Password for Agents offers that access without exposing passwords.<br/>
<br/>
1Password for Agents is rolling out "over the coming days" for Grok Bot and Muse. Claude Duet, ChatGPT Work and Dots, and Town's Townie integrations are "coming soon." <br/>
<br/>
